  "captions": [
    {"start": 0.417, "end": 3.777, "lines": ["Initiated kind","of our own small research program"]},
    {"start": 3.777, "end": 6.857, "lines": ["to follow up and learn","more about things like"]},
    {"start": 7.217, "end": 13.457, "lines": ["we have an ongoing project right now","evaluating how cetaceans specifically,"]},
    {"start": 13.457, "end": 17.777, "lines": ["but marine mammals or surface-breathing","animals more generally are exposed"]},
    {"start": 17.777, "end": 21.057, "lines": ["to oil slicks, for example.","Because one of the things we learned"]},
    {"start": 21.057, "end": 25.377, "lines": ["during the Deepwater Horizon","incident is that the oil that floats"]},
    {"start": 25.377, "end": 30.192, "lines": ["on the surface, we would Classically,","measure the exposure to marine"]},
    {"start": 30.192, "end": 34.352, "lines": ["mammals based on the volatilization","of the oil, how much is evaporating"]},
    {"start": 34.352, "end": 38.752, "lines": ["into the air column, and kind","of base our estimates of exposure"]},
    {"start": 38.752, "end": 41.152, "lines": ["to surface-breathing animals based","on that."]},
    {"start": 41.152, "end": 44.832, "lines": ["But some of the work of Joe Katz","at Johns Hopkins University and others"]},
    {"start": 44.832, "end": 49.312, "lines": ["have documented that when a little bit","of energy hits an oil slick"]},
    {"start": 49.312, "end": 52.392, "lines": ["through like wind","or wave or raindrop action."]},
    {"start": 52.72, "end": 57.2, "lines": ["or say a dolphin br s surfacing","and breathing through the oil"]},
    {"start": 57.2, "end": 61.2, "lines": ["and blowing out through their blowhole","and then rapidly inhaling."]},
    {"start": 61.2, "end": 64.92, "lines": ["Imagine that through an oil slick","and how much oil"]},
    {"start": 65.312, "end": 69.712, "lines": ["Gets forced into the air column","in the form of large droplets, large"]},
    {"start": 69.712, "end": 75.552, "lines": ["watery, oily droplets, small droplets,","and even tiny aerosolized particles"]},
    {"start": 75.552, "end": 79.792, "lines": ["is something that we hadn't explored","very often and certainly hadn't factored"]},
    {"start": 79.792, "end": 80.832, "lines": ["into our exposures."]},
    {"start": 80.832, "end": 85.6, "lines": ["And so now we've got some","ongoing research to assess how much."]},
    {"start": 85.6, "end": 89.92, "lines": ["Water droplets a dolphin produces","during a breathing event without oil,"]},
    {"start": 89.92, "end": 93.2, "lines": ["that we've done","at the National Aquarium at Baltimore."]},
    {"start": 93.2, "end": 96.96, "lines": ["And we've got high-resolution","videography documenting what they produce"]},
    {"start": 96.96, "end": 100.08, "lines": ["and then what they rapidly inhale","in a breathing event."]},
    {"start": 100.08, "end": 104.32, "lines": ["And then we've taken that into the lab","at Johns Hopkins University,"]},
    {"start": 104.32, "end": 106.88, "lines": ["and we are working","on a mechanical structure"]},
    {"start": 106.88, "end": 112.736, "lines": ["that can essentially reproduce a dolphin","breathing event in a laboratory."]},
    {"start": 112.736, "end": 116.256, "lines": ["And then we will add oil on top","of that with and without dispersant"]},
    {"start": 116.256, "end": 119.536, "lines": ["to be able to characterize","and quantify how much is produced"]},
    {"start": 119.536, "end": 124.896, "lines": ["and how much is aspirated directly","into a dolphin blowhole as an example."]},
    {"start": 124.896, "end": 129.296, "lines": ["Yeah, that was the first thing I thought","of when you mentioned a dolphin surfacing"]},
    {"start": 129.296, "end": 134.576, "lines": ["and going to breathe and expelling water","and oil up, but then breathing it back in."]},
    {"start": 134.576, "end": 139.152, "lines": ["So they're actively breathing in this oil,","and there's really no way around it."]},
    {"start": 139.152, "end": 144.432, "lines": ["Yeah, and it it's it's like aspirating","droplets directly into their blowhole."]},
    {"start": 144.432, "end": 147.712, "lines": ["And you could see the pictures","of the marine mammals swimming"]},
    {"start": 147.712, "end": 150.992, "lines": ["in heavy oil,","and it just was heartbreaking."]},
    {"start": 150.992, "end": 154.192, "lines": ["And I hope that that would change","the way we measure oil"]},
    {"start": 154.192, "end": 156.672, "lines": ["in the air column moving forward."]},
    {"start": 156.672, "end": 159.152, "lines": ["And we've got another","project that is looking"]},
    {"start": 159.152, "end": 161.792, "lines": ["at the air-water interface."]},
    {"start": 161.792, "end": 166.592, "lines": ["that air column directly above a slick","to help us understand a little bit"]},
    {"start": 166.592, "end": 171.472, "lines": ["more about how that exposure occurs","to other surface breathing animals."]},
    {"start": 171.472, "end": 177.232, "lines": ["Another aspect of the Deepwater","Horizon response was a pretty quick"]},
    {"start": 177.232, "end": 180.192, "lines": ["and aggressive human health studies."]},
    {"start": 180.192, "end": 181.712, "lines": ["At the peak of the response,"]},
    {"start": 181.712, "end": 184.592, "lines": ["there were over 50,000 people working","on the cleanup."]},
    {"start": 184.592, "end": 188.032, "lines": ["So there's been some long-term studies","of those individuals,"]},
    {"start": 188.032, "end": 191.432, "lines": ["including I volunteered","to be tracked by that."]},
    {"start": 191.856, "end": 195.696, "lines": ["And looking at what kind","of exposure people may have had,"]},
    {"start": 195.696, "end": 199.056, "lines": ["and then not just oil exposure,","but also the other"]},
    {"start": 199.056, "end": 204.736, "lines": ["sorts of collateral impacts related","to stress and overwork and other kinds"]},
    {"start": 204.736, "end": 208.604, "lines": ["of things that we know can cause injuries","to people."]}
  ]
